Original ideas of the author
----------------------------

- A tracker as a live view of REAPER's own timeline: rows are time, columns are
  tracks, every note, item and envelope stays native REAPER data.
- Vim grammar for music editing: modes, operators and motions over notes,
  fields, patterns and modules; a which-key menu for every prefix.
- Patterns as REAPER regions with codes (A1, B2 ...): linked repeats, a pattern
  matrix as the song view, a cube grid of all patterns with glue / split.
- Panes like tmux inside one REAPER script window, every module a pane.
- slixer: a transient slicer / pad sampler JSFX driven 1:1 from the tracker's
  DSP panel - quick slots, a sniper zoom of the slice edge with "spam" roll.
- CONTROL mode: Option+Cmd turns the trackpad into zones over the nearest bank
  of sliders (faders, XY, pan) - no clicking on tiny controls.
- Harmonizer in the tracker: chords from notes and from sound, a chord lane on
  the master as markers, sample pitch as take markers so typing a note
  transposes the sample, negative harmony and neo-Riemannian moves as buttons.
- Microtones in tracker cells (72-EDO marks like C-4^) sent to synths.
- A sample map in the browser: the folder as a graph or a "nebula" of floating
  points grouped into sectors.

Borrowed ideas and code (not the author's own)
----------------------------------------------

- A tracker inside REAPER: the idea of Hackey-Trackey by Joep Vanlier (MIT),
  https://github.com/JoepVanlier/Hackey-Trackey - jf_tracker has its own code;
  its user key file follows Hackey-Trackey's userkeys.lua.
- Parts of jf_tracker are based on Paketti for Renoise by Esa Ruoho (Lackluster),
  used with his permission: https://github.com/esaruoho/paketti
- The reform pane follows the idea of Reform for Renoise (https://www.aqu.surf/reform);
  an own implementation, no code copied.
- The dsp big routing view follows the idea of Sexan's ParaNormal FX Router for
  REAPER; an own implementation, no code copied.
- The Orca field is an own implementation of Orca by Hundred Rabbits (MIT).

